{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The end of all flesh.</b> Everywhere you find sexual immorality and idolatry, calamity comes upon the world and kills good and bad alike." "<b>For the earth is filled with violence.</b> Their decree was sealed only on account of robbery (Sanhedrin 108)." "<b>אֶת הָאָרֶץ.</b> Like מִן הָאָרֶץ, and similar to it: ״כְּצֵאתִי אֶת הָעִיר״ (Micah 1) — from the city; ״חָלָה אֶת רַגְלָיו״ (1 Kings 15) — from his feet. Another interpretation: אֶת הָאָרֶץ — together with the earth, for even three handbreadths of the depth of the plowed furrow were washed away and flattened."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "וע״ז is ועבודה זרה, 'and idolatry'; אנדרולומוסיא is a transliterated Greek term for widespread calamity."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:45.771575604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}